From baeba07ad64fbd749910476f79a0ebdf4d665f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:36:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(cl,motion,post,app,ui): Probe operation - face,
 edge, corner and bore/boss centre finding

A touch-probe tool kind (stylus ball + length, PRB-0400 in the starter
catalog) and a Probe operation seated at 13 to close the Drilling run
(v50 -> v51 pin rung). Modes: face (+-X/+-Y/-Z), edge, outside corner
(two touches), bore and boss centre (four touches). Each touch is a
fast seek, a back-off and a slow measuring re-probe; the path opens with
a positioning rapid and the touches ride Toolpath::probes (cl::ProbeTouch),
filed in the path cache.

The post writes TOUCH / RETREAT / FOUND records: fanuc.cps voices them
as G38.2 (NIST RS274NGC), an incremental G91 back-off, the deviation and
its tolerance stop (#3000) and either G10 L2 Pn (set G54..G59) or a
#3006 operator stop; a probe section starts no spindle or coolant. A
script without onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult refuses the
op by name. The stylus path is judged as protected moves against the
model (a ball nearer than its radius anywhere is a Gouge, holding the
post); probe ops remove no stock. Op page with an original icon.

Owed: creating the op from a picked face/edge/vertex/cylinder (the
contact is typed today), the stylus shank in the protected-move law,
probing hooks for the other dialects.

Refs #108

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
