From 2c686c6478cd7fc72e781fc22a75d26c0301682b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:32:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(probe): program the stylus tip, not the ball centre

The probe path stated the ball centre while every other ball tool
states the tip, and a spindle probe's length register is gauged to the
ball's bottom. The default -Z face op therefore read every face r high
(alarming on tolerance 0.5), and with a looser tolerance G10 L2 moved
the work zero r into the part - every following op cut r too deep.

probe_cycle still plans on the ball centre and now lays every move
point and probe target down at the tip (centre - r along +Z); the safe
plane is a tip height. stylus_hits sweeps the ball about each point
raised by r, so the judged geometry is unchanged. A -Z touch on a face
at Z 20 now posts G31 Z15 (overtravel 5) and expects its trip at Z 20.

Pinned by probe_op::the_posted_g31_z_is_the_tip_at_the_expected_contact
(face and bore-centre modes); the probe_bore_centre golden moves every
Z 2 mm down except the safe plane. Decision in docs/decisions/108-probe.md.

Refs #108

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
